  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">KE IDEAl_LOKA Fest</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Loka Festival brings together the indigenous and ethnic minorities with diverse communities and cultures in Mabera Sub County, Migori County to a one of a kind annual extravaganza to pilot how celebrating cultural diversities through art in faith and freedom can enhance feminism. The project will start at each of the 4 wards of Mabera Sub County as a competition among identified groups that will battle out for the first position in the three categories-two for adult men and women and one for youth. Each organized group comprising of men and women will have one Traditional sacred song appreciating the diversity of the different faiths in the sub countyand a folk tune with a gender inclusive theme.

Each organized group comprising of men and women will have one Traditional sacred song appreciating the diversity of the different faiths in the sub county and a folk tune with a gender inclusive theme. There will be a reserve Youth Category, where the contest will be to get the best choral verse, per ward, that promotes political tolerance, cohesion and the right to vote. Winners per category at the ward level will proceed to produce one entry to advance to the Sub county level for the grand finale. There will be gifts presented and recognition at each level supported by the grant. There will also be the production of creative audio-visual content in the form of recordedmusic and other formats that will be shared on digital platforms.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="90">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IDEAL RESEARCH CENTRE</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ideal Research Centre was founded in 2012 as a response to the need to deliver high quality and innovative development programmes that are underpinned by deep contextual knowledge and human-centered solutions among communities in Western Kenya.  Ideal&apos;sgoal is tocatalyze sustainable development through enhancing institutionalc apacity, establishing partnerships to conduct evidence-based research, Advocacy, and dissemination of information on the policy aspects of the application of science and technology. Based in KisumuCounty, Ideal is able to serve the Counties in the Lake region economic bloc. Our four-thronged pillar approach emphasizes that robust Human Rights approaches and systems embedded in inclusion, rule of law, social justice, and equity devoid of corruption. IRC values community ownership, participation and collaboration to deliver its mandate while taking a systems approach as a preferred pathway towards effecting sustainable change and development among communities. Our vision is  for Sustainable healthy livelihoods and mission is to carry out and implement research-based interventions in the sectors of Health, Agriculture, Governance and Climate Change and inculcate communities and governments to utilize science, technology, and innovation for sustainable development.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
